      "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\n# Round\nkasegi-shokunin round 39, wave 2 (falsify), dispatched by the L1 (agent KasegiR39) via the inline spawn handoff (hyaku run 9). Lane repo /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin is the ONLY lane repo. The fleet root /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin is read-only to you — never write there. /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokuknow is read-only — never write there, never run its campaign tools. Base commit 480b1a505a2dfc14a4f718d16d63808247214d0a; claims-freeze commit dcd31701720a6a4929a32471a62011ed87103421; frozen claims at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-39/claims.json (read it first; do not edit) and claims-erratum-1.md (E1 registry after-count 59; E2 r38 judged head full hash; E4 verification ref Y = J + receipt; E5 non-vacuous measurement semantics). Wave 1 landed the C1 suite and the C2 artifacts; your attack targets are the LANDED bytes in the lane tree (read them at HEAD) plus the frozen predicates in claims.json. You are an ATTACK seat: your job is to falsify the claims as frozen, find defects in the landed work, and verify the do-nothing controls; you are NOT the author of the work (a seat that wrote the deliverable under attack must say so and focus on a different item).\n\nFrozen claims (summary; claims.json is authoritative):\n- C1 depth:verifiability (4, held): r39-closure.sh suite prints `closed=8/8 exit=0` at J and graded `selftest cases=8 failures=0`; base/r38-head reds; G1 whole-tail, G2 graded receipt, G3 committed-run truth, G4 seat identity, G5 no-final-label, G6 scratch quiescence, G7 ledger fill, G8 pinned r37 bytes.\n- C2 coverage (7, held): F22 S057 admission counters (frontier 22, registry 58, knowledge 51, harness 25/25, binding 46/46, audit expected=51, census exit 0, junk-f22 rejected).\n\nRead your item spec below fully before acting. You are a leaf seat (no subagent spawning). Work only your item. No placeholders or plan text — land real evidence: commands you ran with their actual output.\n\nWrite scope. Your ONLY allowed writes are (1) your receipt at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-39/wave2/<SEATNAME>.md (write it last), (2) byte-exact deliverable files your item names, written beside the receipt as /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-39/wave2/<SEATNAME>.<suffix>, and (3) scratch under your scratch dir. Every `Report:` trailer path is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin — write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/<that path>. Never edit any other file in the lane repo, the fleet repo, sibling lane repos, or source trees. Never run a mutating git/jj command anywhere (no add/commit/push/checkout/reset/stash, no jj mutations); read-only git is fine. Never edit MANIFEST.json, templates/, scripts/ (fleet), .ufo/state/, .ufo/watchdog.log, .scratch/, or any sibling repo.\n\nScratch. Create S=/fast/scratch/hyaku/kasegi-r39/<SEATNAME>/ with mkdir -p; bind ALL scratch/work copies there (TMPDIR=$S, --work under $S); never rely on an inherited TMPDIR; /tmp only for files under 50 MB. Remove your scratch dir before you yield (`trap 'rm -rf -- \"$S\"' EXIT`), after copying receipts/deliverables into the wave dir. Do not run a heavy pass while the disk guard is not green.\n\nTooling. Tooling authorization (operator 2026-10-19): you may install/upgrade tools that help the task, after reading /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md (official channels only; record tool/version/channel/reason in your receipt). pacman transactions are PAUSED host-wide — never run pacman; use `uv tool install`, `npx`, or an official binary into ~/.local/bin instead. Never edit ~/.omp/agent/config.yml or mcp.json. Never restart a host service.\n\nHost guard (SEAT_GUARD). Your tools start at the fleet root: cd to your scratch first and use absolute paths for every read/write. If you build a git fixture, create it as D=$(mktemp -d) && git -C \"$D\" init -q and verify `git -C \"$D\" rev-parse --show-toplevel` equals \"$D\" before any commit; never use a throwaway git identity anywhere else. Never write to any PATH directory. Never write fleet-root tracked files.\n\nRules. Keep moves that improve an axis and harm none. Do not message agent://all. Do not run your own swarm. A seat keeps the route chain it captured at spawn. Network fetches: `curl -sS -L --max-time 90 -A kasegi-shokunin/1.0`; record HTTP status, bytes and the UTC fetch time. Godspeed posture governs your work: name the axes, iterate cheap in parallel, keep moves that improve any axis and harm none, never stall in clarifying-question loops.\n\nReview the LANDED r39-closure.sh on the integrated lane tree (read /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/instruments/r39-closure.sh in full; read claims.json C1 and the freeze controls). Verify each G-limb implements the frozen predicate: G1 whole-tail declarations equal added lines + fence model covers ``` and ~~~ + corrections only outside fences + declared paths exist in export; G2 all-gates v3 receipt shape + graded case lines (positive=pass AND verdict=pass required; summary-only never satisfies); G3 committed-run truth (no quoted run without transcript unless report-only); G4 seat identities distinct == tasks, zero-task red; G5 no Final lane commit in round-39 section, judged head by reference; G6 scratch quiescence fail-closed; G7 ledger section filled; G8 pinned r37 bytes + digest-gated. Run the suite yourself on a scratch work dir: `bash corpus/instruments/r39-closure.sh --export-ref <J> --work $S` (expect closed=8/8 exit=0), `--selftest --export-ref <J>` (expect 8 graded case lines, failures=0), base/r38-head exports red, plain run exit 2. Verdict per limb: conformant / defect (with receipts). Receipt only. Leaf seat. Report: .ufo/waves/round-39/wave2/RevSuiteDesign.md\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability\nMilestone: round-39\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-39/wave2/RevSuiteDesign.md"
